+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
@@ -65,9 +65,31 @@ files are read. A pinned adapter model catalog remains labelled as such, not acc
 
 Kimi Code membership uses its official third-party API-key endpoint, not a copied official-client OAuth identity.
 
-The existing template registry distinguishes subscription accounts, subscription plan keys and
-ordinary API services. Optional `category: subscription-plan` is presentation metadata on a
-template, not a credential type or another connection store. Plan templates retain regional
+The provider picker presents one entry per explicitly declared vendor, with search and a custom
+provider action. Cindy supplies vendor-first selection; the owner's follow-up requires no dialog
+or dropdown for choosing a connection. NewMax's installed model setup keeps selection and the
+connection form in one content slot. Fleet therefore replaces the gallery in place with a local
+setup draft: visible service/plan choices, regional choices only when multiple regions exist,
+then address and segmented API formats, followed by the existing multi-key controls. The visual
+values/primitives remain ZCode's. Subscription choices show account connection instead of API fields.
+Selecting a vendor or switching a route never writes a Provider. Back discards only the local
+setup draft. Existing providers and their credentials are not changed. An explicit Add persists
+API credentials through the existing initialConfig facade; explicit Connect continues through
+the existing subscription control. No automatic model inference or paid validation is introduced.
+
+Optional template catalog metadata declares vendor identity/name, service identity/name and
+region. The existing schema, template and facade carry it; grouping is only a UI projection.
+Legacy category remains readable but no longer determines presentation. Templates without
+metadata remain independent. Search matches vendor and variant names in both locales.
+Service/region changes select only declared routes and keep drafts isolated by template ID, so
+keys do not silently cross regions or API/subscription boundaries. Protocol switching among
+explicit route variants selects the actual matching template; custom API configuration remains
+available. Creation has an immediate local lock, preserves the draft/error on failure and retries
+only the selected route. Invalid or removed selections cannot create a different provider.
+Regression checks cover route reachability, locale search, domain roundtrip, draft validation and
+credential isolation. Native desktop inspection checks the in-place choices and existing editor.
+
+Plan templates retain regional
 endpoints and explicit API-key authentication: GLM, Kimi Code, MiniMax Token Plan, Alibaba Coding
 Plan / Token Plan, MiMo Token Plan and OpenCode Go. China/global keys are not interchangeable;
 existing saved instances are never rewritten by template updates. Empty catalogs remain manual
